3. [OPEN] item 94 — PythonStdioRunner fallback. In-process PythonRunner cannot
   reach servers that build the MCP object inside `main()`/a factory/`__main__`,
   so importing the module leaves the FastMCP registry empty. Log signature:
   "Failed to start runner: Could not find callable tool ... (server instance:
   none found; registered tools: [])" -> the config bails BEFORE LLM selection,
   so it shows as fast (~3s) llm=unknown in the run summary.
   IMPACT (measured 2026-09-18, gpt41-corpus run): **592 of 1980 python configs
   (~30%) fail this way** -- blender-mcp, aliyun/hologres, jvm-mcp-server, ~40
   repos. Those python targets are NOT fuzzed at all. Not a regression, not a
   silent-0 (each logs the ERROR honestly), but 30% of python coverage is lost.
   FIX: when in-process discovery returns registered tools:[], spawn the server
   as a subprocess + fuzz over MCP stdio (like the node path). Coverage-blind but
   the oracle still fires. Deferred by Ananto 2026-09-18 (let the current run
   finish first). ALSO: copy the "Failed to start runner" reason into the index
   `error` field so these read as in-process-discovery-failed, not bare llm=unknown.

