## item 17 (2026-09-26): "high-confidence (succ>=0.5)" tier WITHDRAWN (Ananto's call)
- exec_success_rate = n_success/n_exec over ALL of a tool's fuzz executions: a
  reachability measure computed by our harness, not a fuzzer confidence. The silent-bug
  oracle already requires the tool to accept the specific flagged input, so how often it
  rejects other (random) inputs says nothing about a given alert; filtering on it would
  discard real bugs in tools that reject most fuzz inputs.
- Removed as a tier/filter from: eval/triage_findings.py (rate kept as a descriptive
  column; --strong gone), RESULTS_SUMMARY.md, repo24 + recovery reports,
  head_to_head_per_repo, CASE_STUDY_CANDIDATES, sec6_eval.tex (clause commented out,
  378/126 succ>0 split kept). Dated snapshot docs got a "tier withdrawn" note instead
  of rewritten history. Candidate totals unchanged (627 / 129 / 56).
- Paper: report whole candidate counts + hand-verified precision (owed); the rate may
  appear only as a reachability description, never as confidence.

