## item 23 (2026-09-27): PRECISION of the 508 headline -- LOW. Read before citing any bug count.
- findings/labels_20260927/: stratified seeded sample of 98 of 508 (census of small classes;
  only bugs with surviving evidence: 466/508). Labelled from evidence + code at pinned commit,
  read-only, 6 sub-agents + coordinator reconciliation (RUBRIC.md lists every override).
- Weighted over 507 (creds unlabelled): STRICT 12% +-6% (~61 bugs) bug-exists view;
  3% +-2% (~14) alert-grounded view. LENIENT (TP+TP-low) 30% +-8% / 21% +-7%.
- Per class (bug-exists strict/lenient): reflected-xss 5%/14%, log-inj 20%/35%, path-trav 6%/56%,
  ssrf 44%/44%, temp-file 0/17%, cmd-inj 0/50%, exfil 0/0.
- ROOT CAUSES (instrument defects, fixable):
  (1) check_reflected_output fires on template-brace echoes ({{, ${) with no markup, into plain
      text/JSON/errors -- 32/37 xss FP. Fix: require real markup; brace-only is not reflection.
  (2) log-injection: CR/LF comes from the tool's own tracebacks / pydantic / pretty JSON / remote
      error pages, not from the input -- most of 13/20 FP. Fix: require the CR/LF to be in the input
      (provenance, same as the strict SSRF rule).
  (3) outcome oracle on tools that bailed out early (not connected, missing binary/creds) --
      input never reached the sink. Fix: require evidence the sink was reached.
  (4) data-exfiltration: tool's own credential file + its own API call (FP), and downloaded-file
      writes misclassified as exfil (really uncontained writes).
- DO NOT cite "508 bugs" as bugs. Cite candidates + measured precision, or fix (1)-(3) and re-run.
